          }
        ],
        "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: May I ask you a preliminary question, Ms. Mahoney?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ef3713675d99-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask this, what is your response to the, one of your earlier questions. Suppose they sent out a general brochure to all the graduating grammar school students to -- advertising that they come up to Brentwood and so forth and so on, and the rule prohibited that? Would that rule be valid?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ef3713675d99-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, cHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: I'm sorry; you think it might be a reasonable or unreasonable?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ef3713675d99-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, jUSTICE KENNEDY: It seems to me that, turning to the state action for a moment, one of the justifications for finding state action that is there is no other real choice, that they have, other than to -- if they want to play athletics in Tennessee other than to join this association."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ef3713675d99-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, jUSTICE ALITO: What if the state set up two athletic leagues and one had an anti\u2011recruiting rule and the other didn't, and they were equally strong, and you chose to join the one that had the anti\u2011recruiting league. Would it be a violation of the First Amendment in your opinion?"
      }
